notes.body:
Some routines do things such as

```
int
pcap_set_promisc(pcap_t *a, int b)
{
	ws_assert(has_wpcap && p_pcap_set_promisc != NULL);
	return p_pcap_set_promisc(a, b);
}
```

but `pcap_set_promisc()` is a non-optional routine, so if it's not present, the load will fail and `has_wpcap` will be set to `false`. Would `ws_assert(has_wpcap)` suffice?

